# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user

# Editor and IDE state. None of these exist today; they are listed so the first one to appear
# does not get committed by a `git add .`.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Decompiled game source — NEVER commit this. It is MegaCrit's copyrighted code.
# Decompile locally with:  ilspycmd -p -o <dir> "<install>\data_sts2_windows_x86_64\sts2.dll"
sts2src/
decompiled/
*.pck
sts2.dll

# Game art — NEVER commit this either. The web UI's "bundled" asset provider reads from
# assets/, which the operator populates locally. Extracted icons are cached to a temp dir
# outside the repo. See docs/web_app_specs.md section 4.
#
# The two extension globs are deliberately unscoped. Narrowing them to assets/ would let art
# through from anywhere else, and the cost of the broad rule is only that a screenshot in one of
# these formats needs `git add -f`. Wrong in the safe direction.
assets/
*.ctex
*.webp

# Save files, in case one is ever copied in for debugging. These carry a Steam ID and a profile
# path, so they are personal data as well as game data.
*.save

# Personal dev notes. The queue and its reasoning are mine; docs/web_app_specs.md is NOT here,
# because the source comments point at its section 4 for the asset-provenance boundary and a
# clone needs to be able to read it.
docs/plan.md

# Local Claude settings. Load-bearing: settings.local.json records approved paths, which include
# a Steam ID and a home directory.
.claude/
